// Per-user access tier (Settings/Users feature). Orthogonal to the
// better-auth org role on Member.role (owner/admin/member): this axis
// gates WHAT a user can do (write / settings), not the org-plugin role.
//   super    — full access incl. Settings
//   advanced — all access EXCEPT Settings
//   user     — read-only everywhere (can see, cannot mutate)
enum AccessTier {
  super
  advanced
  user
}

// Vendor's interaction mode with a facility, set per facility–vendor
// connection. This axis is about whether the FACILITY'S DATA flows to the
// vendor — nothing else.
//
//   two_way  = the facility's actuals (COG/purchasing) are shared with the vendor.
//   one_way  = they are not; the vendor self-serves from its OWN COG.
//
// 2026-07-28: the previous comment also claimed one_way meant "no facility
// approval ... nothing flows to the facility". Those two clauses can only both
// hold when a contract names NO facility, and both contradicted this enum's own
// field comment on Connection.mode ("the facility's actuals do NOT flow to the
// vendor") and the settings UI ("facility data is not used"). Worse, code briefly
// keyed contract AUTO-ACTIVATION off one_way — which is the FAIL-SECURE default
// for a brand-new connection, so the most restrictive setting silently became the
// most permissive one on a different axis. Whether a vendor may publish a live
// contract into a facility's tenant is now its own facility-granted permission:
// Connection.autoActivateContracts.
enum ConnectionMode {
  one_way
  two_way

  @@map("connection_mode")
}

